  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="eqsiqsis-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">איקסיקסיס</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾyqsyqsys</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">eqsiqsis</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">adjective</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="eqsiqsis-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>measureless</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ἐκσηκωσις</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>לכל תכלה ראיתי קץ וגו' לכל יש סיקוסים השמים והארץ יש להם סיקוסים, חוץ מדבר [G 101: 7 מדבר אחד איקסיקסיס] שאין לו סיקוסים, ואיזו זו זו התורה</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">10,1</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">G 101: 7</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">סיקוסים</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>I have seen an end to every purpose (tiklah), but Thy commandment is exceeding broad (Ps. 119,96): everything has a measure, heaven and earth have a measure, except one measureless thing which has no measure: and what is it? The Torah ... (cf. Freedman / Simon I 71)</quote>
                  </cit>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>In G, probably the original reading. Cf. Sokoloff, G ad loc.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Sperber (1974)</title>
                  <citedRange>125</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
